{"authored" [{"question" "q-139969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $B$ be a matrix with $12$ columns and $4$ non-pivot columns, with enough rows for the $8$ required pivots ($m\\ge8$). What is $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)$?\n\nHint: Each non-pivot column corresponds to a free variable. Check that the required pivot count can fit in the number of rows." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/review.json" "file_sha256" "cbda6e7b787fd73762bdf5c0e02d3c6dcad2ba9620f7671e7aa6d87b643d979c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "fc3db58fc0bc360771f96974305d8c34698ce762d74ab10257287b8076dc73d5" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/verification.json" "basis" 2302 "rationale" "Four non-pivot columns among twelve require eight pivot columns. Rank cannot exceed row count, so seven rows are infeasible. Keep the core nullity question and answer 4, requiring only derived m≥8 rather than inventing a specific replacement row count. Preserve field and answer identities because their values do not change."} {"question" "q-139969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Each non-pivot column corresponds to a free variable in $Bx=0$, so the null space has dimension equal to the number of non-pivot columns. There are $4$ such columns, hence $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)=4$.\n\nThe pivot count is $12-4=8$, so $\\operatorname{rank}(B)=8$. Rank-nullity confirms $\\dim\\operatorname{Null}(B)=12-8=4$. A matrix with this rank must have at least $8$ rows. This is feasible for any row count $m\\ge8$; for example, put eight pivot columns and four zero columns in an $m\\times12$ matrix.\n\nThe original source specified a $7\\times12$ matrix with $4$ non-pivot columns. That would require $8$ pivots in only $7$ rows, contradicting $\\operatorname{rank}(B)\\le7$. No such original matrix exists. The corrected study question states the derived row requirement without choosing an arbitrary replacement row count. The original prompt, revealed answer $4$, worked solution and grade remain preserved as source evidence." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/review.json" "file_sha256" "cbda6e7b787fd73762bdf5c0e02d3c6dcad2ba9620f7671e7aa6d87b643d979c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "fc3db58fc0bc360771f96974305d8c34698ce762d74ab10257287b8076dc73d5" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/verification.json" "basis" 2302 "rationale" "Four non-pivot columns among twelve require eight pivot columns. Rank cannot exceed row count, so seven rows are infeasible. Keep the core nullity question and answer 4, requiring only derived m≥8 rather than inventing a specific replacement row count. Preserve field and answer identities because their values do not change."} {"question" "q-139969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/review.json" "file_sha256" "cbda6e7b787fd73762bdf5c0e02d3c6dcad2ba9620f7671e7aa6d87b643d979c" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "fc3db58fc0bc360771f96974305d8c34698ce762d74ab10257287b8076dc73d5" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-139969/verification.json" "basis" 2302 "rationale" "Four non-pivot columns among twelve require eight pivot columns. Rank cannot exceed row count, so seven rows are infeasible. Keep the core nullity question and answer 4, requiring only derived m≥8 rather than inventing a specific replacement row count. Preserve field and answer identities because their values do not change."} {"question" "q-139970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $W$ be a $9\\times 10$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $W?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(W))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $W.$ \n\nSince $W$ has $10$ columns and $8$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $W$ is \n\n$$\n10-8=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(W))=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacad