the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34904" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.jso