asis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(D)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))$, we reduce $D$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5606ebf5f1faebbaffe824e7acbab6e7e461c64b72d4531435a2c3f726ca433" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-35345" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mat