/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/state.json" "file_sha256" "ce9b68f635c51e00917f68e2fd3eece137cc866428907b1aa168dfb2bf1adeee" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5419.json" "file_sha256" "011328f9089cd45396b8ee4cb71596812aeb592123bf4ed885085befbfd0dfb2" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n11-9=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5419.json" "file_sha256" "011328f9089cd45396b8ee4cb71596812aeb592123bf4ed885085befbfd0dfb2" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/62cc7238e6676b8a43d216ab6c8b30504602c68fd548832eceac9b710b885471.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/b85d717afa8af39d10517f909a09b53e6d379beef6e04e3d9ce7d3e48c88dca4.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\n- If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/8e12a5386c3db2149324bd28c174a5410f7751e0c963cf80969e0cfdf14e5d7b.png) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5421.json" "file_sha256" "6697ee091479547bd7fc8010eac92def0dad5eb754f0e38ceb518963c169859d" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5421.json" "file_sha256" "6697ee091479547bd7fc8010eac92def0dad5eb754f0e38ceb518963c169859d" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/assets/e20df1b44d2bfe100499eebfb4d2bdf8c1055978fdccbe11c8b5c0882052ace8.png) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5422.json" "file_sha256" "c0ac8852b651c33761e644728627a394d3cbae0cb0f757752086287688a2f9c1" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/example-5422.json" "file_sha256" "c0ac8852b651c33761e644728627a394d3cbae0cb0f757752086287688a2f9c1" "basis" 2301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068410/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-34914" [] "q-79196" [] "q-139975" [] "q-139973" [] "q-35317" [] "q-139969" [] "e-5422" [] "q-34902" [] "q-35345" [] "q-34900" [] "q-35316" [] "e-5421" [] "q-34906" [] "q-79339" [] "q-139970" [] "q-34904" [] "q-34973" [] "e-5419" []} "basis" 2302 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186121703 17592186121704 17592186121705 17592186121706 17592186121707 17592186121709 17592186121710 17592186121711 17592186121712 17592186121713 17592186121775 17592186121776 17592186121777 17592186121778 17592186121779 17592186123869 17592186123870 17592186123871 17592186123872 17592186123873 17592186357545 17592186357546 17592186357547 17592186357548 17592186357549 17592186357552 17